# Who can place and remove scenes

## Default

- **Everyone** can place scenes.
- **Everyone** can remove their **own** scenes.
- **Police, sheriff and marshal** jobs, and the **admin** group, can remove **any** scene.

## Limit placing to some jobs

1. Open **/poggy** → **Poggy Scene** → **Access & permissions**.
2. Turn on **Job lock**.
3. Add the jobs that may place scenes to **Allowed jobs**.
4. Save and restart.

If **Allowed jobs** is empty, Job lock does nothing: everyone can still place.

Players who are blocked see the text **Scene blocked** (by default "Cant place scene in hideout"). You can change it in **Text & language**.

## Who can remove any scene

Add jobs to **Remove jobs**. These jobs can also always place scenes, even with Job lock on.

Players in the `admin` group can always place and remove. That group name is fixed in the script.

## Good to know

- Job names are **exact** and **case-sensitive**: `Sheriff` is not `sheriff`.
- Every removal is checked again on the server, so players cannot get around it.
- To remove a scene, stand next to it and press **4**.
- Server staff can remove any scene from anywhere in **/poggy** → **Poggy Scene** → **Scenes** (see *Managing scenes in /poggy*).
